($t$Cyamopsis tetragonoloba$t$, $t$Cyamopsis tetragonoloba$t$, $t$Fabaceae$t$, $t$Famiglia botanica: Fabaceae. Portamento: Perennial. Altezza massima indicativa: 2 m. Cluster Bean or Guar (Cyamopsis tetragonoloba) is a legume with a nitrogen-fixing capability due to its symbiotic relationship with certain soil bacteria. It is used in crop rotation to replenish the soil. It is an upright plant that grows up to 3 m in height. The leaves and stems are mostly hairy. The leaves are elongated, oval shaped, and of alternate position. It is often consumed as a vegetable. The seed is the source of guar gum which is used as a stabilizer and thickener in various food and food products. It is also eaten when cooked and possesses medicinal values. It stabilizes blood sugar level, a laxative, and a digestive tonic. The plant is very drought resistant when established.$t$, $j${"luce": "Pieno sole", "acqua": "Moderata", "terreno": "Tollera terreno: sabbioso/leggero, medio"}$j$::jsonb, ARRAY[$t$Scheda in bozza, importata automaticamente da Plants For A Future (pfaf.org): dati non verificati manualmente, da controllare prima di considerarli affidabili$t$, $t$Nome comune (inglese, fonte PFAF): Guar, Cluster Bean$t$, $t$Rischi segnalati dalla fonte (testo originale in inglese, non tradotto per non alterarne il significato): The immature seedpods contain high contents of hydrocyanic acid, though by the time the pods mature this has been reduced to a trace[ 200 ].$t$], $j${"irrigazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "concimazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "potatura": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "npk": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}}$j$::jsonb, $j${"famiglia_botanica": "Fabaceae", "giorni_germinazione": null, "giorni_trapianto": null, "giorni_raccolta": null, "finestra_semina": [], "finestra_trapianto": [], "resistenza_g