($t$Cyperus articulatus$t$, $t$Cyperus articulatus$t$, $t$Cyperaceae$t$, $t$Famiglia botanica: Cyperaceae. Portamento: Perennial. Altezza massima indicativa: 1.8 m. Cyperus articulates or commonly known as Piripiri or Jointed Flatsedge is an aromatic species of sedge in Africa, southern Asia, northern Australia, south eastern United States, the West Indies, and Latin America. It is one of the traditional spices of the Amazon region. It produces stout culms about 250 cm tall from a long-creeping, thick rhizome. The rhizome can be eaten raw when peeled. The plant is used in the treatment of nausea, vomiting, stomach pains, intestinal gas, headaches, colds, flu, mouth sores and ulcers, and hypertension. Externally, it is used to treat snake bites and prevent baldness. Piripiri stems are used in making baskets, mats, sacks, and other crafts. Essential oil from the rhizome is used in perfumery while the rhizome can be dried or burnt and used as incense and as a mosquito repellent. The plant can also be grown along the banks of streams to prevent soil erosion.  It is native to Africa, temperate and tropical Asia.$t$, $j${"luce": "Pieno sole", "acqua": "Pianta acquatica/palustre", "terreno": "Tollera terreno: sabbioso/leggero, medio, argilloso/pesante"}$j$::jsonb, ARRAY[$t$Scheda in bozza, importata automaticamente da Plants For A Future (pfaf.org): dati non verificati manualmente, da controllare prima di considerarli affidabili$t$, $t$Nome comune (inglese, fonte PFAF): Jointed flatsedge, Priprioca, Piripiri$t$, $t$Rischi segnalati dalla fonte (testo originale in inglese, non tradotto per non alterarne il significato): None known$t$], $j${"irrigazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "concimazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "potatura": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "npk": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}}$j$::js