($t$Dacryodes edulis$t$, $t$Dacryodes edulis$t$, $t$Burseraceae$t$, $t$Famiglia botanica: Burseraceae. Portamento: Tree. Altezza massima indicativa: 20 m. Dacryodes edulis, commonly known as Bush Butter Tree, Safou or Atanga, is a fruit tree native to Africa. It is evergreen and usually grows about 18-40 m in height, with a short trunk and a deep, dense crown. The compound leaves are glossy. The bark is pale grey. The flowers are yellow and arranged in a large inflorescence. The fruit is an ellipsoidal drupe and can be eaten raw, cooked, or roasted. Bush butter tree has long been used in traditional medicine to treat wounds, skin ailments, fever, ear trouble, tonsillitis, and dysentery among other conditions. Bark resin is used in perfumery, as an adhesive, as a waterproofing, etc. The tree is sometimes used as an ornamental. The wood of bush butter tree is used for tool handles, mortars, and carpentry.$t$, $j${"luce": "Tollera: pieno sole, mezz'ombra", "acqua": "Abbondante, terreno costantemente umido", "terreno": "Tollera terreno: sabbioso/leggero, medio, argilloso/pesante"}$j$::jsonb, ARRAY[$t$Scheda in bozza, importata automaticamente da Plants For A Future (pfaf.org): dati non verificati manualmente, da controllare prima di considerarli affidabili$t$, $t$Nome comune (inglese, fonte PFAF): Bush Butter Tree, Butterfruit, African Plum, bush pear, bush plum, safou$t$, $t$Rischi segnalati dalla fonte (testo originale in inglese, non tradotto per non alterarne il significato): None known$t$], $j${"irrigazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "concimazione": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "potatura": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}, "npk": {"primavera": null, "estate": null, "autunno": null, "inverno": null}}$j$::jsonb, $j${"famiglia_botanica": "Burseraceae", "giorni_germinazione": null, "giorni_trapianto": null, "giorni_raccolta": null, "finestra_semi